    "title": "Eagles down Flyers in swimming/diving - NewsBreak",
    "text": "13 hours ago The Little Falls Flyers were defeated 106-71 by the St. Cloud Apollo Eagles in swimming/diving on Monday, Sept. 29.\nLittle Falls’ Abi Nagorski finished first in the 100-yard breaststroke with a time of 1:16.95.\nShe was also a member of the Flyers’ 200 medley relay team, which also included Tayla Bowman, Grace Stracka and Ariana Smieja, that placed second with a time of 2:12.57.\nThe Flyers’ Cora Kliber finished second in the 100-yard breaststroke with a time of 1:25.15.\nLittle Falls (0-8) swam at Ogilvie on Thursday, Oct. 2, but no results were available at press time.\nThe Flyers will compete against the Falcons in Foley on Thursday, Oct. 9. Action begins at 6 p.m.",
